<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Geiler von Kaysersberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1445–1510</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Geiler von Kaysersberg was a priest and the most celebrated preacher of late medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, who held the pulpit of Strasbourg Cathedral from 1478 until his death. Raised in Kaysersberg in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, from which he took his name, he attacked clerical abuses and the vices of townspeople in vivid German sermons and pressed for reform of the Church before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-geiler-von-kaysersberg.jpg" alt="Johann Geiler von Kaysersberg" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johannes_geiler_von_kayersberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
